Third-party material
====================

Portions of this repository are adapted from Quantum Machines' qua-libs
(https://github.com/qua-platform/qua-libs), which is distributed under the
BSD 3-Clause License reproduced below. The adapted material is:

- calibrations/01a_time_of_flight.py, 02a_resonator_spectroscopy.py, 03a_qubit_spectroscopy.py,
  08a_readout_frequency_optimization.py,
  04b_power_rabi.py, 05_T1.py, 06a_ramsey.py, 06b_echo.py, 07_iq_blobs.py:
  node structure (description, parameters, QUA program, analysis, state update)
  and the QUA sequences, adapted from
  qualibration_graphs/superconducting/calibrations/1Q_calibrations/. The
  06a_ramsey.py QUA program follows the upstream virtual-detuning program
  closely.
- calibration_utils/time_of_flight.py: the 01a analysis (ADC conversion,
  Savitzky-Golay smoothing, threshold edge detection, offsets and success
  test), adapted from
  qualibration_graphs/superconducting/calibration_utils/time_of_flight/analysis.py.
- calibration_utils/readout_frequency_optimization.py: the 08a analysis (g/e
  separation, trailing rolling mean, chi and success test), adapted from
  qualibration_graphs/superconducting/calibration_utils/readout_frequency_optimization/analysis.py.
- calibrations/90_calibration_graph_bringup.py: node order, adapted from
  90_calibration_graph_bringup_fixed_frequency_transmon.py in the same directory.
- qua/config.py: configuration layout and integration-weight names, adapted from
  Quantum-Control-Applications/Superconducting/Single-Fixed-Transmon/configuration.py.

Each adapted file links the upstream file it follows.

